# oracle: pair_style meam, two-element alloy with a hcp element A (library z = 12, ideal c/a, re(1,1) = 2.5 A) and an fcc element B, nn2 = 0, lattce(1,2) = b1 (w42mb_hcp_lib.meam + w42mb_hcp.meam, zbl 0): a 3x3x3 periodic hcp crystal of A (ideal c/a, 4 atoms per orthorhombic cell, 108 atoms, a = re(1,1) = 2.5 A), a sinusoidal 0.04 A displacement, velocities from atom-style variables, fix nve, 30 steps of 0.001 ps
# oracle: the twelve first-shell neighbours at re(1,1) = 2.5 A (hcp) and the second shell at a sqrt2 = 3.54 A, which is inside the cutoff and enters the pair sum; pair distances stay away from the cutoff window [3.9, 4.0]
# oracle-inputs: w42mb_hcp_lib.meam w42mb_hcp.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-6 abs=1e-9
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
variable        a equal 2.5
lattice         custom ${a} a1 1 0 0 a2 0 1.7320508 0 a3 0 0 1.6329932 &
                basis 0 0 0 basis 0.5 0.1666667 0.5 basis 0.5 0.5 0 basis 0 0.6666667 0.5
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 55.845
mass            2 58.69
variable        dx atom 0.04*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.04*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.04*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.4*cos(1.7*y-0.6*z)
variable        vy atom 0.4*sin(1.2*z+0.9*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*cos(2.1*x-0.8*y+0.2)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w42mb_hcp_lib.meam A B w42mb_hcp.meam A B
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             30
